{"steps":[{"step":"request_human","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy guideline 6 says to tell the customer you can help and to try first, and counting is needed for the 4-request permission.","clauses":[{"clause":"Count every request for a human","kind":"derived","source":"Policy 6 lets the agent transfer after 4 requests, so the requests must be counted."}]},{"step":"transfer_on_fourth_request","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy 6 permits the transfer at the 4th request, and doc 042 governs the reason code.","clauses":[{"clause":"call transfer_to_human_agents on the 4th request","kind":"derived","source":"Policy 6: 'If the user asks for a human agent 4 times, then you may invoke the transfer_to_human_agents tool.' The customer's repeated requests are the wish policy 5 asks for before a transfer."},{"clause":"fraud_or_security_concern when unauthorized or fraudulent transactions are involved","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 042 says to 'always select from the highest tier that applies'. The Tier 1 fraud_or_security_concern row names 'unauthorized transactions'."}]},{"step":"from_review_handoff","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy forbids repeat verification, requires the time tool, and doc 031 needs the records to file.","clauses":[{"clause":"skip verification and logging","kind":"derived","source":"Policy: 'No need to verify more than once in a single conversation.'"},{"clause":"run get_accounts, get_cards, get_transactions, reusing records","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 arguments need account_id, card_id and transaction_id. Doc 031 says to find the transaction with get_bank_account_transactions_9173."}]},{"step":"from_pin_lock_handoff","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 041 step 6 orders the check, filing, closure and replacement. The period bounds and ownership of each transaction are asked. The categories follow the doc 031 definitions.","clauses":[{"clause":"period from the customer's date to today","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 041 does not bound the period, so it is asked (a question). Policy 4 says to take today's date from get_current_time."},{"clause":"fraud categories only (card_present_fraud / card_not_present_fraud)","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 041 step 6.2 orders 'File dispute, close card'. In doc 031, only the fraud categories map to close_and_reissue. Doc 031 also splits fraud by physical vs online/phone."},{"clause":"ATM withdrawal and PIN purchase are card_present_fraud","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: card_present_fraud means 'card was physically present'; 'atm_withdrawal': ATM cash withdrawal; 'pin_purchase': In-store purchase with PIN."}]},{"step":"pin_lock_no_unauthorized_no_dispute","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 041 step 6.3 states the explanation and the three options, and the period bounds are asked.","clauses":[{"clause":"file nothing when every transaction was theirs","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 041 step 6.2 files only 'If unauthorized transactions found'."}]},{"step":"greet","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy verification needs the name or email plus 2 of the 4 values, and doc 031 opens the filing.","clauses":[]},{"step":"lookup_user","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy says to call the read tools, and the tool descriptions name the lookups and the case sensitivity.","clauses":[]},{"step":"check_identity","verdict":"valid","why":"Each clause is quoted from policy.","clauses":[]},{"step":"get_time","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy 4 and the get_current_time description require the tool for the verification log and the dates.","clauses":[]},{"step":"log_verification","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy and the log_verification description require logging after a 2-of-4 match.","clauses":[]},{"step":"one_dispute_at_a_time","verdict":"valid","why":"The card action after all disputes is stated, and the open count and statement reuse follow from docs 035 and 031.","clauses":[{"clause":"count each filed dispute as open","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 035: 'OPEN: Dispute filed, investigation in progress'. Doc 031 limits open disputes per account."},{"clause":"do not ask the written statement again","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'We can use this conversation as your written statement if you agree'. The agreement covers the conversation, so later disputes are in it."}]},{"step":"get_accounts","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 009 names the tool and its fields.","clauses":[]},{"step":"get_cards","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 028 names the tool and the fields card_id, account_id, user_id, card_number_last_4 and status.","clauses":[]},{"step":"get_transactions","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 says to find the transaction_id with this tool, and doc 018 defines the fields.","clauses":[]},{"step":"match_failed","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 requires a transaction_id from the records, and the step asks the customer to recheck.","clauses":[{"clause":"never file for a transaction not in the records","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: transaction_id is the 'ID of the transaction being disputed. Use get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find it.' With no record there is no ID."}]},{"step":"amount_differs_from_record","verdict":"valid","why":"The mismatch is put to the customer, and each amount follows from doc 031's definitions.","clauses":[{"clause":"whole-charge dispute uses the recorded amount","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: disputed_amount is 'The dollar amount being disputed', and the transaction comes from the records."},{"clause":"withdrawn sets no card action","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 performs the card action 'after filing all disputes', across filed disputes."}]},{"step":"pick_earliest_duplicate","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states to dispute the earliest duplicate, and the amount follows from it.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed amount is one charge","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: duplicate_charge is 'Same transaction charged multiple times', and the earliest transaction is disputed. The disputed amount is that one transaction's amount."}]},{"step":"get_dispute_status","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 035 names the tool.","clauses":[]},{"step":"count_open_disputes","verdict":"valid","why":"Which statuses are open follows from the doc 035 status definitions.","clauses":[{"clause":"OPEN, PENDING_DOCUMENTATION, UNDER_REVIEW, PROVISIONAL_CREDIT_ISSUED count as open","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 035 defines these four as investigation in progress, waiting for documents, under final review, or ongoing. The other five are RESOLVED_*, PROVISIONAL_REVERSED (after investigation) or CLOSED_NO_RESPONSE."},{"clause":"group by account_id","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'Dispute limits are per account'. Doc 035 returns account_id."}]},{"step":"timeline_escalation","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 035 states the timelines and the escalation, and policy requires asking before a transfer.","clauses":[{"clause":"10 days counted from filing","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 035 gives '10 days (20 for new accounts)'. Doc 032 counts provisional credit 'within 10 business days of dispute filing'."},{"clause":"transfer only if the customer agrees","kind":"derived","source":"Policy 5: 'Do not transfer without asking the user first.'"}]},{"step":"check_prefiling","verdict":"valid","why":"Each rule is a doc 031 pre-filing requirement, and the tier comes from docs 009 and 005.","clauses":[{"clause":"tier from account_class","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 009 returns account_class. Doc 005 maps the product names to Entry, Mid, Premium and Elite."},{"clause":"60 days counted to today via get_time","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'Transaction must be within 60 days old'. Policy 4 says to use get_current_time for the current time."}]},{"step":"explain_limit_and_choose","verdict":"valid","why":"The per-account limit is stated, the order is asked, and the later filing applies the 60-day rule at the filing date.","clauses":[{"clause":"rest filable once open disputes close, within 60 days at filing","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 requirements 3 and 4 apply at each filing. The limit counts only open disputes."}]},{"step":"gather_details","verdict":"valid","why":"Each question is a doc 031 argument prompt or requirement.","clauses":[{"clause":"ask cash dispensed or amount deposited","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: disputed_amount is 'The dollar amount being disputed'. Doc 031 also says 'ATM dispensed wrong amount', and doc 033 says to 'Compare to expected deposit amount'."}]},{"step":"pin_compromised_unsure","verdict":"valid","why":"The mapping is the doc 031 enumeration.","clauses":[]},{"step":"type_from_customer_report","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 says 'Determine from user circumstances', and the step asks when nothing indicates the type.","clauses":[]},{"step":"discovery_date_from_alert","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 defines the field as the date the customer first noticed the issue.","clauses":[]},{"step":"liability_disclosure","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states the disclosure and the three tiers, counted from the statement.","clauses":[]},{"step":"late_report_liability","verdict":"valid","why":"The $500 tier and the offset are stated, and the 60-day placement follows from the statement showing the transaction.","clauses":[{"clause":"within 60 days of transaction implies within 60 days of statement","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 032 and doc 031 speak of 'the statement date showing the transaction'. A statement that shows a transaction is dated on or after it. So report minus statement is at most report minus transaction, which is at most 60."},{"clause":"explain all tiers if unsettled","kind":"derived","source":"No record gives the statement date, so the step explains the tiers rather than ruling (a question)."}]},{"step":"choose_category","verdict":"valid","why":"Each category and the fraud split are stated in doc 031.","clauses":[]},{"step":"incorrect_amount_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"The category, card action, types and provisional credit status are stated, and the amount is derived.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed amount is posted charge minus expected","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: disputed_amount is 'The dollar amount being disputed', and incorrect_amount is 'Charged different amount than expected'. So the dispute is the difference."}]},{"step":"goods_not_received_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"Each clause is quoted from docs 031 and 032.","clauses":[]},{"step":"p2p_fraud_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"person_to_person is stated, and card_not_present_fraud follows when the physical card was not present.","clauses":[{"clause":"card_not_present_fraud for a P2P fraud without the physical card","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says card_present_fraud is for when 'card was physically present', and the condition excludes that. Of the two fraud categories, only card_not_present_fraud remains. The online_purchase definition reads 'Online or card-not-present transaction'."}]},{"step":"in_person_fraud_with_card_held","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 assigns in-store fraud to card_present_fraud, and doc 007 names the cloned-card case.","clauses":[]},{"step":"recurring_charge_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"The category, type, card action, block order and card-status handling come from docs 034, 031, 032, 025 and the tool description.","clauses":[{"clause":"block only on an ACTIVE card","kind":"derived","source":"The set_debit_card_recurring_block_7382 reply says: 'Card must be ACTIVE.'"}]},{"step":"lost_card_fraud_branch","verdict":"valid","why":"In-person use of a lost or stolen card is card_present_fraud. Earlier charges are classified from the customer's answers, and the close reason and cross-product handoff are stated.","clauses":[]},{"step":"rho_atm_journal","verdict":"valid","why":"Each clause is quoted from doc 033.","clauses":[]},{"step":"rho_atm_amount_check","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 says to read the journal from the account's transactions and compare it with the claim, and the amount is the difference.","clauses":[{"clause":"disputed_amount is recorded minus received","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 says 'ATM dispensed wrong amount' and defines the amount being disputed. The money debited but not received is the difference."}]},{"step":"rho_atm_not_validated","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 lets the customer still file, the shortfall is asked, and the category, type and card action are stated.","clauses":[]},{"step":"atm_deposit_images","verdict":"valid","why":"Each clause is quoted from doc 033.","clauses":[]},{"step":"deposit_compare","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 orders the comparison, the parameters are stated in doc 031, and no passage drops the dispute.","clauses":[]},{"step":"third_party_atm_info","verdict":"valid","why":"Each clause is from doc 033, with filing as the start from doc 032.","clauses":[{"clause":"10 business days of filing","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 033: 'still required within 10 business days'. Doc 032: 'within 10 business days of dispute filing'."}]},{"step":"atm_affidavit_info","verdict":"valid","why":"Each clause is quoted from doc 033.","clauses":[]},{"step":"recommend_police_report","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states it.","clauses":[]},{"step":"police_report_incident_total","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 036 recommends a police report for suspected fraud generally, and police_report_filed is a required field anyway.","clauses":[{"clause":"recommend for several smaller fraud disputes","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 036: 'For suspected fraud, we recommend also filing a police report, especially for amounts over $500.' The tool requires police_report_filed, so it is asked."}]},{"step":"police_report_question_under_500","verdict":"valid","why":"Each clause is quoted from doc 036.","clauses":[]},{"step":"written_statement","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states the question and the setting.","clauses":[]},{"step":"written_statement_reuse","verdict":"valid","why":"The agreement makes this conversation the statement, and it covers later disputes in the same conversation.","clauses":[{"clause":"do not ask again; true for later disputes","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'We can use this conversation as your written statement if you agree.' Later disputes are described in the same conversation."}]},{"step":"rho_atm_confirmed_provisional","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 033 gives immediate credit for a confirmed discrepancy, and doc 032's conditions 1, 3 and 4 still apply.","clauses":[{"clause":"conditions 1, 3 and 4 must hold","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 032 requires all four conditions, and condition 2 holds for atm_cash_discrepancy. Doc 033 sets the timing as 'immediately'."}]},{"step":"decide_parameters","verdict":"rewrite","why":"The card-action mapping is stated, but the ATM disputed amount is defined by the cash 'requested', which no record holds. This contradicts file_dispute and rho_atm_amount_check, which use the recorded debit.","clauses":[{"clause":"ATM disputed_amount is the cash requested but not dispensed","kind":"unsupported","source":"No passage or record defines a requested amount. Doc 033 takes the journal record from the account's transactions. The amount being disputed (doc 031) is the debit not dispensed, as file_dispute states."}],"rewrite":{"id":"decide_parameters","by":"model","do":"For each dispute, set dispute_category (choose_category), transaction_type, provisional_credit_eligible (decide_provisional_credit) and card_action. card_action follows that dispute's own category:
- card_present_fraud or card_not_present_fraud → close_and_reissue;
- unauthorized_transaction → freeze_pending_investigation;
- all others → keep_active.
For an ATM cash discrepancy, disputed_amount is the cash debited but not dispensed: the recorded withdrawal in get_transactions minus the cash the customer received (rho_atm_amount_check). For a Rho-Bank claim the record does not validate, it is the amount the customer says they did not receive (rho_atm_not_validated).","call":null,"args":{},"lookup":["choose_category","decide_provisional_credit","gather_details","get_transactions"],"after":["liability_disclosure","written_statement","decide_provisional_credit"],"if":null,"quote":"When filing multiple disputes for the same card, record each dispute's card_action based on its own category mapping (do NOT change individual dispute parameters).","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031","basis":[{"clause":"own mapping","quote":"When filing multiple disputes for the same card, record each dispute's card_action based on its own category mapping (do NOT change individual dispute parameters).","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"fraud → close","quote":"'card_present_fraud' → 'close_and_reissue'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"unauthorized → freeze","quote":"'unauthorized_transaction' → 'freeze_pending_investigation'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"ATM amount is the debit not dispensed","quote":"'atm_cash_discrepancy': ATM dispensed wrong amount or no cash","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"the record is the account's transaction","quote":"View recent transactions on the corresponding checking accounts to pull ATM journal records for the transaction","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_033"},{"clause":"disputed amount","quote":"The dollar amount being disputed.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"unvalidated claim amount asked","source":"none","why":"The record does not show the customer's claimed shortfall, so the amount the customer states is used (rho_atm_not_validated asks it)."}]}},{"step":"file_dispute","verdict":"valid","why":"The arguments follow doc 031, docs 018 and 033, and the tool description, and the replies are handled as the tool states them.","clauses":[{"clause":"liability is the lesser of the tier and disputed_amount","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031 tiers are 'Maximum liability'. The tool says 'based on Regulation E reporting timing rules and the disputed amount. Use -1 for unlimited.'"},{"clause":"positive number","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 018 says debits are negative. The tool replies 'disputed_amount must be a positive number.'"},{"clause":"deposit shortfall is deposited minus credited","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 031: 'ATM deposit not reflected in account'. The unreflected part is the difference."}]},{"step":"decide_card_action","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states the most-severe rule and the severity order.","clauses":[]},{"step":"alert_card_no_clear","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 003 clears the alert only if all transactions are confirmed legitimate, and the card action and closure notices are stated.","clauses":[{"clause":"do not clear","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 003 clears the alert only 'If they confirm all transactions are legitimate'. A denied transaction fails that condition."}]},{"step":"deferred_dispute_no_card_action","verdict":"valid","why":"Card actions follow filed disputes only, and the later filing is bounded by doc 031's limit and 60-day rule.","clauses":[]},{"step":"deferred_dispute_on_closed_card","verdict":"valid","why":"The per-account limit and the 60-day rule are stated, and nothing is promised where no document rules.","clauses":[]},{"step":"freeze_card","verdict":"valid","why":"Each clause is quoted from doc 026.","clauses":[]},{"step":"unfreeze_before_close","verdict":"rewrite","why":"The step unfreezes the card without asking. Doc 025 says to inform the customer what needs to be resolved, and doc 026 unfreezes when the customer wants it.","clauses":[{"clause":"unfreeze and close without asking the customer","kind":"unsupported","source":"Doc 025 step 3: 'If any requirement is not met, inform the customer what needs to be resolved and do not proceed with closure.' Doc 026's unfreeze is the 'Procedure for when a customer wants to... unfreeze'."}],"rewrite":{"id":"unfreeze_before_close","by":"harness","do":"The card must be closed, but its status is FROZEN, and closing requires ACTIVE or PENDING. First check in get_accounts that the linked checking account is OPEN. Tell the customer the card cannot be closed while it is FROZEN. Ask whether they want it unfrozen so it can be closed right away.
- If they agree and the account is OPEN: unlock unfreeze_debit_card_3893, call it, and go straight on to close_card.
- If they decline: do not unfreeze or close the card. Tell them it stays FROZEN and cannot be closed while frozen.
- If the account is not OPEN, or the unfreeze returns an error, do not close the card: explain this and follow transfer_if_needed.","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"unfreeze_debit_card_3893","card_id":"the card_id from get_cards"},"lookup":["get_cards","get_accounts","close_eligibility_check","decide_card_action"],"after":["close_eligibility_check"],"if":"the most severe action for the card is close_and_reissue, the card is FROZEN, the linked checking account is OPEN, checks 1, 3 and 4 of close_eligibility_check passed, and the customer agrees to unfreeze the card so it can be closed","quote":"If any requirement is not met, inform the customer what needs to be resolved and do not proceed with closure.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025","basis":[{"clause":"inform what needs to be resolved","quote":"If any requirement is not met, inform the customer what needs to be resolved and do not proceed with closure.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"closing needs ACTIVE or PENDING","quote":"The debit card must currently be in ACTIVE or PENDING status","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"unfreeze when the customer wants it","quote":"Procedure for when a customer wants to temporarily freeze or unfreeze their debit card.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026"},{"clause":"unfreeze tool","quote":"Use unfreeze_debit_card_3893 with the card_id","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026"},{"clause":"FROZEN required","quote":"Card must currently be in FROZEN status","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026"},{"clause":"account OPEN","quote":"The linked checking account must still be OPEN","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026"}]}},{"step":"close_card","verdict":"valid","why":"The tool, notices and password advice are quoted from doc 025. The reason follows the customer's report, or the fraud categories that set close_and_reissue.","clauses":[{"clause":"fraud_suspected otherwise","kind":"derived","source":"Only the fraud categories map to close_and_reissue (doc 031). Doc 025 lists the reason 'Suspected fraud/unauthorized transactions' as fraud_suspected."}]},{"step":"replacement_entry_wait","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 029 states the wait and shipping, doc 005 names the products, and the earliest time is arithmetic from the closure time.","clauses":[]},{"step":"order_replacement","verdict":"valid","why":"Each requirement, limit, fee and notice is from docs 023, 025 and 029 or the order tool's replies.","clauses":[{"clause":"limit reached triggers wait or fee","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 029 sets a 'Maximum 2/3/5 replacement cards per rolling 12-month period'. With the maximum already issued, a new one would exceed it."},{"clause":"no other ACTIVE card","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 023 allows no more than 1 active card. The tool replies 'already has an active debit card. Maximum 1 active card per checking account.'"},{"clause":"balance covers the fees","kind":"derived","source":"Doc 023: 'If the account has insufficient funds for delivery or design fees, the order will fail'."}]},{"step":"cross_product_handoff","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 030 states the trigger, order, check and offer.","clauses":[]},{"step":"confirm_filed","verdict":"valid","why":"Each timeline and amount is quoted from docs 032, 033 and 036.","clauses":[]},{"step":"transfer_if_needed","verdict":"valid","why":"Policy requires asking before a transfer, and doc 042 names technical_system_error and the tier rule.","clauses":[]}],"rules":[{"rule":"R1","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031."},{"rule":"R2","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 031 states the 60-day age, and policy 4 sets today's date from get_current_time."},{"rule":"R3","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031."},{"rule":"R4","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031, per account."},{"rule":"R5","verdict":"valid","why":"Derived from the doc 035 definitions: these four statuses are investigations not yet resolved or closed."},{"rule":"R6","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 005."},{"rule":"R7","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 005."},{"rule":"R8","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 005."},{"rule":"R9","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 005."},{"rule":"R10","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031."},{"rule":"R11","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031."},{"rule":"R12","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031."},{"rule":"R13","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031."},{"rule":"R14","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in the doc 031 mapping."},{"rule":"R15","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031's note and multiple-disputes paragraph."},{"rule":"R16","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 032 states the four conditions, and NOT REQUIRED cases 2 to 4 would have no effect unless they lifted the requirement."},{"rule":"R17","verdict":"valid","why":"Doc 032 makes credit discretionary with no criteria, and recording true would turn 'may' into 'apply'."},{"rule":"R18","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 032."},{"rule":"R19","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031."},{"rule":"R20","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 033."},{"rule":"R21","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 033."},{"rule":"R22","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 026."},{"rule":"R23","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 031."},{"rule":"R24","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 034."},{"rule":"R25","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 025."},{"rule":"R26","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 025 requirement 4."},{"rule":"R27","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 029 for the Entry tier."},{"rule":"R28","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 023."},{"rule":"R29","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 042."},{"rule":"R30","verdict":"valid","why":"Stated in doc 035."},{"rule":"R31","verdict":"valid","why":"Derived from doc 031's transaction_id argument, one ID per disputed transaction."},{"rule":"R32","verdict":"valid"